  "branchtag": "a373059428e99856f41716fd2ebe58b1f8da7c8b",
  "classes": [
    {
      "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:d40c5903f1a46a871f6b129da49fa85e4610a4f1021b8b7553d37be4fa67b3a5",
      "@type": "Class",
      "apDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Collectie van Observaties met dezelfde kenmerken."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Collection of Observations with the same characteristics."
        }
      ],
      "apLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Observatieverzameling"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Observation collection"
        }
      ],
      "apUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Bv Observaties die op hetzelfde tijdstip plaatsvonden of hetzelfde Object observeren of door dezelfde sensor zijn gemaakt."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "E.g. Observations that took place at the same time or observe the same Object or were made by the same sensor."
        }
      ],
      "assignedURI": "http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/ObservationCollection",
      "diagramLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Observatieverzameling"
        }
      ],
      "scope": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/scope/External",
      "status": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard",
      "vocLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Observatieverzameling"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Observation collection"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:402dae2f484f9b3827aa07100820f699e4c6fd21427c0c7825fdaeccc29cc82c",
      "@type": "Class",
      "apDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Object on which or along which traffic occurs or that is part of traffic."
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Object waarop of waarlangs zich verkeer voordoet of dat deel uitmaakt vh verkeer."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Object on which or along which traffic occurs or that is part of traffic."
        }
      ],
      "apLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "TrafficObject"
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Verkeersobject"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "TrafficObject"
        }
      ],
      "apUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "ATTENTION: This class is abstract, it must be specialized as a TrafficDomainObject or as a TrafficSamplingObject. As a Traffic DomainObject if the measurement directly relates to the object you want to observe (e.g. a RoadSegment or a Vehicle, etc.) or as a TrafficSamplingObject if the measurement is done indirectly (e.g. via a TrafficMeasuringPoint located along a RoadSegment)."
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "OPGELET: Deze klasse is abstract, ze moet gespecialiseerd worden als Verkeersdomeinobject of als Verkeersbemonsteringsobject. Als Verkeersdomeinobject als de meting direct betrekking heeft op het object dat men wil observeren (bvb een Wegsegment of een Voertuig etc) of als Verkeersbemonsteringsobject als de meting onrechtstreeks gebeurt (bvb via een Verkeersmeetpunt gelegen langs een Wegsegment). OPMERKING: Meer info over deze klasse in applicatieprofiel <a href=\"https://data.vlaanderen.be/doc/applicatieprofiel/verkeersmetingen\">Verkeersmetingen</a>."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "ATTENTION: This class is abstract, it must be specialized as a TrafficDomainObject or as a TrafficSamplingObject. As a Traffic DomainObject if the measurement directly relates to the object you want to observe (e.g. a RoadSegment or a Vehicle, etc.) or as a TrafficSamplingObject if the measurement is done indirectly (e.g. via a TrafficMeasuringPoint located along a RoadSegment)."
        }
      ],
      "assignedURI": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/verkeersmetingen#Verkeersobject",
      "diagramLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Verkeersobject"
        }
      ],
      "parent": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:c03be8a6cb31eaf3a661d6b0c5c5da28d48df28bcf09ce41ef1e2e2c90917cb9"
        }
      ],
      "scope": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/scope/inPublicationNamespace",
      "status": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard",
      "vocDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Object waarop of waarlangs zich verkeer voordoet of dat deel uitmaakt vh verkeer."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Object on or along which traffic occurs or that is part of traffic."
        }
      ],
      "vocLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Verkeersobject"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Traffic object"
        }
      ],
      "vocUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "OPGELET: Deze klasse is abstract, ze moet gespecialiseerd worden als Verkeersdomeinobject of als Verkeersbemonsteringsobject. Als Verkeersdomeinobject als de meting direct betrekking heeft op het object dat men wil observeren of als Verkeersbemonsteringsobject als de meting onrechtstreeks gebeurt (bvb via een Verkeersmeetpunt)."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "ATTENTION: This class is abstract, it must be specialized as a Traffic Domain Object or as a Traffic Sampling Object. As a Traffic Domain Object if the measurement is directly related to the object that one wants to observe or as a Traffic Sampling Object if the measurement is done indirectly (e.g. via a Traffic Measurement Point)."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:c03be8a6cb31eaf3a661d6b0c5c5da28d48df28bcf09ce41ef1e2e2c90917cb9",
      "@type": "Class",
      "apDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Object uit de reële wereld dat geen Bemonsteringsobject is."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Real-world object that is not a Sampling Object."
        }
      ],
      "apLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Domeinobject"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Domain object"
        }
      ],
      "apUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Dit is het werkelijk geobserveerdObject. Als rechtstreeks observeren niet kan observeren we een representatief staal, het zgn Bemonsteringsobject. In dat geval is het Domeinobject het bemonsterdObject. OPMERKING: Deze klasse is louter informatief, in praktijk moet ze gesubstitueerd worden door een klasse uit het domein. Bv in het domein Waterkwaliteit zou het domeinobject een instantie vd klasse Rivier kunnen zijn."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "This is the actual observed object. If direct observation is not possible, we observe a representative sample, the so-called Sampling Object. In that case, the Domain Object is the sampledObject. NOTE: This class is purely informative, in practice it must be substituted by a class from the domain. E.g. in the Water Quality domain, the domain object could be an instance of the class River."
        }
      ],
      "assignedURI": "http://def.isotc211.org/iso19156/2011/GeneralFeatureInstance#GFI_DomainFeature",
      "diagramLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Domeinobject"
        }
      ],
      "scope": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/scope/External",
      "status": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard",
      "vocLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Domeinobject"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Domain object"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:aee3360ffd1cdf7fa7d25eb302613fe16998beee14a54d99e20c4b51da81fc2d",
      "@type": "Class",
      "apDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Determining the value of a certain feature of the traffic at a certain point in time or between two points in time."
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Het vaststellen van de waarde van een bepaald kenmerk van het verkeer op een bepaald tijdstip of tussen twee tijdstippen."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Determining the value of a certain feature of the traffic at a certain point in time or between two points in time."
        }
      ],
      "apLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "TrafficMeasurement"
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Verkeersmeting"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "TrafficMeasurement"
        }
      ],
      "apUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Traffic is defined as the movement of objects such as people, freight, data, etc. over modes such as land, water, air, cables. In the context of this application profile, by traffic we mean road traffic. Traffic can refer to objects that move themselves (with or without a means of transport) or objects that are transported, but also to objects over which traffic takes place. The measurement can be the determination of the value of a feature of an individual Vehicle or TrafficParticipant during its movement (e.g. its speed or license plate) or of a feature of the infrastructure such as a RoadSegment or a Lane over which the traffic moves (e.g. the traffic intensity ). TrafficMeasurements are Observations, in other words there is a certain margin of error on the value due to the measuring technique used."
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Verkeer wordt gedefinieerd als de verplaatsing van objecten zoals personen, vracht, data etc over media zoals land, water, lucht, kabels. In de context van dit applicatieprofiel bedoelen we met verkeer het wegverkeer. Verkeer kan betrekking hebben op objecten die zichzelf verplaatsen (al dan niet met een vervoermiddel) of objecten die vervoerd worden, maar ook op objecten waarover verkeer plaatsvindt. De meting kan het vaststellen van de waarde van een kenmerk van een individueel Voertuig of Verkeersdeelnemer tijdens zijn verplaatsing zijn (bvb zijn snelheid of nummerplaat) of van een kenmerk van de infrastructuur zoals een Wegsegment of een Rijstrook waarover het verkeer zich beweegt (bv de verkeersintensiteit). Verkeersmetingen  zijn Observaties, maw op de waarde zit een zekere foutmarge door de gebruikte meettechniek. OPMERKING: Meer info over deze klasse in applicatieprofiel <a href=\"https://data.vlaanderen.be/doc/applicatieprofiel/verkeersmetingen\">Verkeersmetingen</a>."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Traffic is defined as the movement of objects such as people, freight, data, etc. over modes such as land, water, air, cables. In the context of this application profile, by traffic we mean road traffic. Traffic can refer to objects that move themselves (with or without a means of transport) or objects that are transported, but also to objects over which traffic takes place. The measurement can be the determination of the value of a feature of an individual Vehicle or TrafficParticipant during its movement (e.g. its speed or license plate) or of a feature of the infrastructure such as a RoadSegment or a Lane over which the traffic moves (e.g. the traffic intensity ). TrafficMeasurements are Observations, in other words there is a certain margin of error on the value due to the measuring technique used."
        }
      ],
      "assignedURI": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/ns/verkeersmetingen#Verkeersmeting",
      "diagramLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Verkeersmeting"
        }
      ],
      "parent": [
        {
          "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:4003b79e21603e1229273e0c500f0b31b29d880bfb80ad2c543ff90d252d68f3"
        }
      ],
      "scope": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/scope/inPublicationNamespace",
      "status": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard",
      "vocDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Het vaststellen van de waarde van een bepaald kenmerk van het verkeer op een bepaald tijdstip of tussen twee tijdstippen."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Determining the value of a particular feature of traffic at a specific point in time or between two points in time."
        }
      ],
      "vocLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Verkeersmeting"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Traffic measurement"
        }
      ],
      "vocUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Verkeer wordt gedefinieerd als de verplaatsing van objecten zoals personen, vracht, data etc over media zoals land, water, lucht, kabels. In de context van dit applicatieprofiel bedoelen we met verkeer het wegverkeer. Verkeer kan betrekking hebben op objecten die zichzelf verplaatsen (al dan niet met een vervoermiddel) of objecten die vervoerd worden, maar ook op objecten waarover verkeer plaatsvindt. De meting kan het vaststellen van de waarde van een kenmerk van een individueel Voertuig of Verkeersdeelnemer tijdens zijn verplaatsing zijn (bvb zijn snelheid of nummerplaat) of van een kenmerk van de infrastructuur zoals een Wegsegment of een Rijstrook waarover het verkeer zich beweegt (bv de verkeersintensiteit). Verkeersmetingen  zijn Observaties, maw op de waarde zit een zekere foutmarge door de gebruikte meettechniek."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Traffic is defined as the movement of objects such as people, cargo, data etc over media such as land, water, air, cables. In the context of this application profile, traffic refers to road traffic. Traffic can refer to objects that move themselves (with or without a means of transport) or objects that are transported, but also to objects over which traffic takes place. The measurement can be the determination of the value of a characteristic of an individual Vehicle or Road User during its movement (e.g. its speed or number plate) or of a characteristic of the infrastructure such as a Road Segment or a Lane over which the traffic moves (e.g. the traffic intensity). Traffic measurements are observations, in other words there is a certain margin of error on the value due to the measurement technique used."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:4003b79e21603e1229273e0c500f0b31b29d880bfb80ad2c543ff90d252d68f3",
      "@type": "Class",
      "apDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Het vaststellen van de waarde van een bepaald kenmerk van een Object op een bepaald tijdstip of tussen twee tijdstippen."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Determining the value of a particular feature of an Object at a specific time or between two points in time."
        }
      ],
      "apUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Het gaat om schattingen van de waarde,maw op de waarde zit een zekere foutmarge. Voorbeelden zijn temperatuur,klasse,kleur. Dit is verschillend van waarden die zijn toegekend en dus geen schattingen zijn zoals naam of prijs."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "These are estimates of the value, in other words, there is a certain margin of error on the value. Examples are temperature, class, color. This is different from values that have been assigned and are therefore not estimates such as name or price."
        }
      ],
      "assignedURI": "http://def.isotc211.org/iso19156/2011/Observation#OM_Observation",
      "diagramLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Observatie"
        }
      ],
      "scope": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/scope/External",
      "status": "https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard",
      "vocLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Observatie"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Observation"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "urn:oslo-toolchain:928a3cd63ead8eef8cbf928f5c3df5b374d0cba02cbab9e6eabdeaa7023d90bf",
      "@type": "Class",
      "apDefinition": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Device or Agent (including Persons or software) with which Observations are made."
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Toestel of Agent (incl Personen of software) waarmee Observaties gemaakt worden."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Device or Agent (including Persons or software) with which Observations are made."
        }
      ],
      "apLabel": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Sensor"
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Sensor"
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Sensor"
        }
      ],
      "apUsageNote": [
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Sensors generate a result based on a stimulus, i.e. a change in the environment, or based on results from other Observations. They are typically hosted by a Platform. Examples are speedometers, gyroscopes, barometers, magnetometers mounted on a smart phone. The human eye, for example, can also be regarded as a Sensor."
        },
        {
          "@language": "nl",
          "@value": "Sensoren genereren een resultaat op basis van een Stimulus, ttz een verandering in de omgeving, of op basis van resultaten van andere Observaties. Ze worden typisch gehost door een Platform. Voorbeelden zijn snelheidsmeters, gyroscopen, barometers, magnetometers gemonteerd op een smart phone. Ook bv het menselijk oog kan beschouwd worden als een sensor."
        },
        {
          "@language": "en",
          "@value": "Sensors generate a result based on a stimulus, i.e. a change in the environment, or based on results from other Observations. They are typically hosted by a Platform. Examples are speedometers, gyroscopes, barometers, magnetometers mounted on a smart phone. The human eye, for example, can also be regarded as a Sensor."
        }
      ],
      "assignedURI": "http://www.w3.org/ns/sosa/Sensor",
      "diagramLabel": [
        {
          "@value": "Sensor"
        }
      ],
